   Asked one second after the cancel, LangGraph said: run 01a19642 is interrupted.
   From then on the agent sent 8 more updates. The task is a plain (synchronous) function running in a thread of its own: the cancel stops LangGraph waiting for it, not the function, so it runs on while the run reads interrupted.

